-- title:
--   Reading an oriented crossing chart in the geometric function field
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M$ with $p \mid M$, $p^2 \nmid M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing every unit whose image in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ is trivial, a witness $hj$ that `jqModC ℚ` lies in the field $\mathrm{qExpFunctionFieldC}\ \mathbb{Q}\ \top$, and a bundle $\mathfrak{X} :$ `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $A$, with algebraically closed residue field of characteristic $p$, let $\rho : R_p \to A$ be a ring map compatible with $R_p \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain with $R_p \to O$, maximal ideal $(p)$, a residue map $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa_A$ over $\rho$, an embedding $j_O : O \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ over $R_p$, and $\iota_A : O \to A$ lifting $j_O$ and inducing $\mathrm{to}\kappa$. Fix a point $n$ of the fibre product of `𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ 0` and `𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ 1`, and write $x_n$ for its image in $X_O = X_{R_p} \times_{R_p} \operatorname{Spec} O$ under the first projection followed by `𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ 0` and `bcMap`. Assume given $e \ge 1$, an open $U \ni x_n$ of $X_O$ and $f : U \to \operatorname{Spec}\bigl(O[X_0,X_1]/(X_0X_1 - p^e)\bigr)$ over $\operatorname{Spec} O$, such that: the two distinguished elements `CrossingQuotient.U (p^e)` and `CrossingQuotient.V (p^e)` both lie in the prime $f(y)$ exactly when $U.\iota(y) = x_n$; at every $y$ over $x_n$ the stalk map of $f$ is flat, carries the maximal ideal onto the maximal ideal and induces an isomorphism of residue fields, and $f$ is étale on some open neighbourhood of $y$ in $U$; and, as an orientation condition, `V (p^e)` lies in $f(y)$ precisely when $U.\iota(y)$ lies in the image of `𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ 0 ≫ bcMap`, while `U (p^e)` lies in $f(y)$ precisely when $U.\iota(y)$ lies in the image of `𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ 1 ≫ bcMap`. Let $\mathrm{pr}_J : X_{\overline{\mathbb{Q}}} \to X_O$ be the base change of $\operatorname{Spec} j_O$, and let $g_v, g_u \in \Gamma(X_O, U.\iota(\top))$ be the global sections of $U$ obtained by pulling back `V (p^e)` and `U (p^e)` along $f$. The assertion is that the generic point of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Meta}.C$ lies in the preimage of $U.\iota(\top)$ under $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{eeta}$ followed by $\mathrm{pr}_J$, and that, for the ring map $\mathrm{read}$ sending a section to the class in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \cdot F(\Gamma_H(M)) =$ `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` of its germ at that generic point (pull back along $\mathrm{pr}_J$ and $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{eeta}$, take the germ, transport by $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Meta}.\mathrm{ffEquiv}^{-1}$), the elements $\mathrm{param} = \mathrm{read}(g_v)$ and $\mathrm{param}' = \mathrm{read}(g_u)$ satisfy: (1) $\mathrm{param}\cdot\mathrm{param}' = p^e$; (2) both `𝔛.ξzero` and `𝔛.ξinf` lie in $U.\iota(\top)$, and there the germ of $g_v$ is a unit at `ξzero` and lies in the maximal ideal at `ξinf`, while the germ of $g_u$ is a unit at `ξinf` and lies in the maximal ideal at `ξzero`; (3) every $\sigma \in \mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ lying in the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ and fixing $j_O(o)$ for all $o \in O$ fixes $\mathrm{param}$ and $\mathrm{param}'$ under the semilinear action `arithmeticGalois (xHFunctionField M H)`; and (4) for every place $W$ of `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ whose residue field is generated by $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, every section $s : \operatorname{Spec} A \to U$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\iota_A$ whose composite with $U.\iota$ restricts along `barPt A` to the point of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Meta}.C$ corresponding to $W$ under `pointEquivPlace`, followed by $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{eeta}$ and $\mathrm{pr}_J$, and every ring map $\chi : O[X_0,X_1]/(X_0X_1-p^e) \to A$ with $s$ followed by $f$ equal to $\operatorname{Spec}\chi$, both $\mathrm{param}$ and $\mathrm{param}'$ lie in the valuation subring of $W$ and $W.\mathrm{evalAt}\,\mathrm{param} = \chi(V(p^e))$, $W.\mathrm{evalAt}\,\mathrm{param}' = \chi(U(p^e))$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$.
--
--   This converts an oriented étale chart of the Deligne–Rapoport model at a crossing point of the special fibre into a pair of elements of the geometric function field of $X_H(M)$ which multiply to $p^e$, behave as a local parameter and its companion at the two generic points of the special fibre, are invariant under the relevant inertia, and whose values at rational places are computed by the chart. It is the reading step used by the subsequent results constructing annuli of width $e$ attached to the two ends and identifying the corresponding parameters.
